+3. deleted pack → CtxPackDeleted;
+4. pack-read and attach rights BOTH checked (deny each, assert error);
+5. fragment text appears only in the stored capsule reference summary — never in the
+   result object or error messages (sentinel test with `CTXPACK_SECRET_SENTINEL_7812`);
+6. materialize does NOT change usage counters (recordUse never called — spy).
+7. snapshot: zero attachments → empty v1 snapshot; duplicate capsule IDs reject; hash
+   mismatch rejects whole snapshot; 9 attachments reject; over-budget rejects; one
+   denied reference rejects ALL (no partial snapshot); order preserved (attachments +
+   fragment ordinals); snapshot has no reusable grant fields; after snapshot returns,
+   delete the pack + mutate repository rows → snapshot object unchanged (immutability);
+   diagnostics recorder receives bytes/counts only (sentinel absent from recorder).
+
+## 8. Gates
+
+```bash
+cd packages/core && $BUN test --only-failures test/ctxpack-materialize.test.ts
+cd packages/core && $BUN test --only-failures test/ctxpack-capability.test.ts
+```
+
+## 9. HANDOFF (`packages/core/src/ctxpack/HANDOFF-X1.md`)
+
+Format: Base commit / ## Files changed / ## Tests / ## Public exports / ## Central
+integration actions / ## Assumptions / ## Known limitations / ## Prohibited-pattern scan.
+Central integration actions (list, do NOT do): M1 composes CtxPackMaterializer into the
+core Layer and into the P1 materialize handler; Q1 imports `snapshotForSessionInput` and
+`SessionContextSnapshot` exactly.
+
+Reply with: files changed, what was implemented, what was left undone or uncertain.
